WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.250
CapSense is a single volume soft haptic
input/output device that provides

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.360
integrated and simultaneous contact
force sensing and vibrant tactile

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:16.500
feedback. Since we have information about
the driving waveform magnitude, we can

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.760
carry out concurrent pressure sensing by
monitoring the voltage across HapSense.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:26.730
Our device system fully supports
portability, where HapSense can even

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:34.020
be operated with a small lithium polymer
battery. HapSense is a ferroelectric

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.940
polymer actuator which can operate at
relatively low voltage compared to

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.200
existing software actuators, which we
introduce a low-temperature fabrication

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.940
process to allow HCI practitioners to
build their own soft haptic input/output

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.890
devices. Conductive electrode patterns
were manually screen printed on the

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:58.670
prepared PVDF film. Patterned adhesive
film was applied to form a single unit

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:04.110
study 25 units were stacked on each
other. We carried out thorough

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:08.729
electromechanical characterizations to
ensure HapSense's performance as an

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:14.159
actuator and a sensor. We demonstrate
example applications where we highlight

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:18.330
a single volume soft interface that can
provide simultaneous haptic sensing

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:23.009
capability. HapSense can be attached to a
syringes plunger to train users to

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:27.479
maintain a constant injection rate. By
sensing the applied force on the plunger,

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:31.560
vibrotactile feedback with distinctive
waveforms can be provided to correct the

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.620
users injection rate.
When controlling a virtual object, it is

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.540
not often clear whether input commands
have been processed or missed. HapSense can

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.980
vibrate when a user successfully execute
a tap or press gesture to select a 3d

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:49.930
model in a mixed reality environment.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:54.560
Multiple HapSense prototypes can be
configured to support private and

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:00.800
ice-free interactions. In this example,
users get macro-level vibration from a

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.120
phone. By placing their hands on the
prototype, users can acquire detailed

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.790
information through spatio-temporal
vibration patterns. We devised 2x2 arrays

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:16.640
of HapSense to configure a haptic
notification panel. Users can acquire

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.050
information from specific software
applications such as the calendar app by

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.140
placing their hand on different
locations of multiple HapSense

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.280
prototypes. Input commands can be
executed simultaneously by simply

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.850
pressing different regions of the system.
HapSense can be adapted to various

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:36.230
mounting surfaces including uneven
profiles with soft and flexible material

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:40.850
properties. The furniture's armrests can
be used as both a remote controller and

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:45.980
a smartphone-connected vibration panel.
We can embed HapSense on various soft

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:52.400
surfaces, such as a smartphone case, due
to its low profile and soft form. Adding

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.000
a soft input/output device onto a
smartphone case will not only add

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.300
sensing functionality, but also localized
vibrotactile feedback.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.220
By augmenting contact sensing with
integrated vibrotactile feedback we hope

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.819
to expand and improve the means of
interactions with soft input/output

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:18.120
devices.

